        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I've made several attempts to make it possible to write custom surrounding that would support this fully, but I don't think it is possible without changing 'mini.surround' code. The main problem is that for linewise selection left surrounding is applied to the [first non-blank character](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/a4241b6f51393d5e4d91a12d94e386bae287dae5/lua/mini/surround.lua#L1765-L1767). If it wasn't the case, then the following would work:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.surround').setup({\r\n  custom_surroundings = {\r\n    -- Use `<CR>` as surrounding identifier\r\n    ['\\r'] = { output = { left = '\\n', right = '\\n' } },\r\n  },\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nCurrently, it will affect the indentation of first selected line.\r\n\r\nAs present behavior of special handling of indent in linewise selection seems to be more universally applicable, I don't think this will be possible in 'mini.surround'. I'd suggest using my previous advice on custom mapping or combination of `go`/`gO` from 'mini.basics'.",
