            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "After looking at the source (thanks for your well written code!), I found a partial solution/workaround:\n\n```lua\nrequire('mini.surround').setup({\n  custom_surroundings = {\n    ['\\r'] = {\n      output = function()\n        local indent = vim.api.nvim_get_current_line():match('^(%s*)')\n        return { left = '\\n' .. indent, right = '\\n' }\n      end\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nSurrounding a whole line with `<CR>` will work fine (and it's my only use-case).\n\nHowever, the line before will always have the indentation, and I don't know if I can get rid of this with the current settings. I tried to replace the whole line with the same without indent, before returning `{ left, right }`, and it does funny but irrelevant things.\n\nSo, with '·' representing the space indentation, the following line:\n\n```\n····Hello world!\n```\n\nwould become\n```\n····                <- Indentation only\n····Hello world!    <- Text keeping its indentation\n                    <- Empty line\n```",
